Silo patch 0011 — xinput: keep controllers working across hotplug (Wine's rework of the device handling)

Origin: Zagrios/voile-wine (Obelisk's Wine, built on crossover-sources-26.3.0), commit d21b3c3f (2026-09-26,
author Zagrios), a backport of 16 Proton's Wine commits (ValveSoftware/wine, listed in the original message below)
without their Steam Input / overlay hacks, and without a4b109236160 (it rescans every HID device on each
XInputGetState() for an empty slot). License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, like Wine. Hunks unchanged.

Why Silo carries it: a quality fix taken on its merit (user, 2026-11-14), not a fix for a measured game. One lock
guards opening/reading/removing controllers, the polled state is read without it, the read event survives
unplug/replug (it leaked), a failed read keeps the previous state, and pads report native xinput's capabilities.
The xinput1_1/1_2/1_3/1_4 Makefile.in hunks add XINPUT_VER defines; xinput9_1_0 is touched too. Applies cleanly on
top of 0002–0010 and builds with no warnings. Tried 2026-11-14 on FATAL FURY (2492040): no effect there — the game
never calls XInputGetState (it reads pads through Raw Input/HID).

---- original commit below (git format-patch, unchanged) ----

From d21b3c3f54969a8308e383e90e761eb7fdce6287 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zagrios <40181755+Zagrios@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:31:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xinput1_3: Keep controllers working across hotplug.

Take Wine's rework of xinput's device handling: one lock guards opening,
reading and removing controllers, the state games poll is read without
that lock, a read event survives unplugging and replugging (it leaked
before), and a failed read keeps the previous state while the packet
number still advances. Controllers also report the capabilities native
xinput reports, which some games check before treating a pad as an Xbox
one. From Proton's Wine: 64ca68c68d6c, be051c83ce1c, db523be38ee2,
6ed81b409a2b, e472645d3626, b75aefe0af54, cc6995fb6942, 9d9af04b4175,
cc872c292bf5, 3d357607b058, 5dd7fffd3018, 372b18c931ca, 39a71b7a4aba,
8e646fedba09, 32034f5bf63e and 37d87f860174 (ValveSoftware/wine), without
their Steam Input and Steam overlay hacks. a4b109236160 is left out: it
rescans every HID device on each XInputGetState() call for an empty slot,
which games make for all four slots every frame.
